  "provider": "codex-cli:gpt-5.6-sol:medium",
  "raw": "{\"judgements\":[{\"id\":\"T1\",\"kind\":\"contradiction\",\"quotes\":[\"- `rules.http_router_backend` (56 routes, Factory `300bd11d` … `a6916180314d`)\\n  — router closure and router context (`70_router_closure.json`,\\n  `70_router_context.json`).\",\"- **Route table** is `rules.http_router_backend` (56 routes, 49 table and 7\\n  irregular, in the accepted spec; 50 and 43 since the six challenge routes\\n  left on 2026-11-07, R0-23) instead of the former `rules.http_route_catalog`; administrator\\n  project discovery `GET /admin/projects` is added (R0-08).\"],\"later_state\":null,\"precedent\":null,\"divergence\":\"One implementation binds all 56 rows still attributed to `rules.http_router_backend`; another binds the revised 50 routes, so an HTTP client observes whether a removed challenge route is mounted.\",\"why\":\"State 2 still attributes 56 routes to the current named backend, while State 5 says that same backend has 50 after six challenge routes were removed.\",\"witness\":{\"initial\":\"The post-R0-23 service is being assembled from `rules.http_router_backend`.\",\"events\":[\"The deployment process calls `runtime.create_runtime_app`.\",\"`api.create_app` binds every row of `rules.http_router_backend` exactly once.\",\"An HTTP client requests one of the six former challenge routes.\"],\"outcomes\":[\"The 56-route backend mounts the challenge route and dispatches it.\",\"The revised 50-route backend has no such route, so the request is unmatched.\"],\"observer\":\"The HTTP client\",\"basis\":[\"### Callers\\n\\n`boundary:deployment_process`.\",\"R0-10 and R0-11: exactly one `PortalStore` from `settings.database_url`; one\\ninner application from `api.create_app`; liveness at `/health/live` and\\nreadiness at `/health/ready`, each answering exactly `HealthStatus`; the\\ntransport guard installed before mounting; the inner application mounted at\\n`/api` and then at `/`. It implements no transport policy itself.\",\"`rules.http_router_backend`: every route row bound exactly once — staff,\\nadministrator and producer bearer routes by the table, the seven viewer-cookie\\nroutes by `api_irregular` — binary rows answered as plain responses, and one\\nexception handler per `error_policy` mapping available to the module, any\\nother failure the policy default (500).\",\"On 2026-11-07 the owner removed the staff email challenges (`00_product.md`\\nR0-23): the former `flow:deferred_staff_challenges`, its six routes (the\\nroute table keeps 50 of the 56 routes of `rules.http_router_backend`) and the\\nemail modules are gone, and staff login and session resolution accept an active account without\\na separate verified-email condition (`02_rules.md` A3).\"]},\"bases\":[{\"passage\":\"- `rules.http_router_backend` (56 routes, Factory `300bd11d` … `a6916180314d`)\\n  — router closure and router context (`70_router_closure.json`,\\n  `70_router_context.json`).\",\"rests_on\":\"\"},{\"passage\":\"- **Route table** is `rules.http_router_backend` (56 routes, 49 table and 7\\n  irregular, in the accepted spec; 50 and 43 since the six challenge routes\\n  left on 2026-11-07, R0-23) instead of the former `rules.http_route_catalog`; administrator\\n  project discovery `GET /admin/projects` is added (R0-08).\",\"rests_on\":\"On 2026-11-07 the owner removed the staff email challenges (`00_product.md`\\nR0-23): the former `flow:deferred_staff_challenges`, its six routes (the\\nroute table keeps 50 of the 56 routes of `rules.http_router_backend`) and the\\nemail modules are gone, and staff login and session resolution accept an active account without\\na separate verified-email condition (`02_rules.md` A3).\"}]}]}",
  "later_documents": {
   "80_notes.md": "734e5fd2535136372d21742dd20e0d69ed65833fc578b80b7cae5ffe0f2c793f"
  }
 },
